  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tarocchi Siciliano. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tarocchi Siciliano (Sicilian Tarot) is a traditional card game played with a unique 63-card deck. It features ranks and suits distinct from other Tarot decks (Portuguese-style pips). The game is a point-trick game, often played by 4 players. Features the 'Fugitive' (Fool) and 'Miseria' (low trump).",
    objective: 'Take more than half the card points (55 or more of 109) in tricks; win last trick (Vanto) and other bonuses (Pigliata, 4 Re, Arie) for jochi. Soloist plays alone against the others; in 4-player, caller may name a trump to get a secret partner.',
    gameplay: 'Must follow suit. Must trump if void. Fugitive (Fool) is excuse. Trumps 20-1 (highest to lowest), plus Miseria (lowest).',
    keyRules: [
      'Unique deck (Portuguese pips)',
      'Miseria trump',
      'Fugitive excuse',
    ],
